# Issue #3314: reproduce the timer registration's circular eligibility.
# Foreground writes populate a warm cache but never advance its checkpoint.
# The timer asks for a checkpoint before scheduling the read that earns one.
# Activation and scheduling fairness stay intact. With no stop required,
# an active leaf retains its acknowledged WAL forever.
# The live advance (#5572) discharges that starvation for any leaf it can
# advance, so this mutant runs in the world #3314 lived in: no leaf is born
# (BOUNDS), so every populated leaf has the timer replay's fairness, and the
# live advance is removed (the second edit, declared). It is classified in the
# refinement note as removing an action.
MODULE: ReclamationEventuallyAdvancesWarmLeafNeedsCheckpoint
TARGET: ReclamationEventuallyAdvances
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: a warm leaf needs a persisted checkpoint before its timer is registered to schedule replay
PERTURBS: ScheduleReplay, LiveAdvance
BOUNDS: MaxFaults = 0, BornAtInit = FALSE

--- FIND
    /\ cache[l] # {} \/ (cache[l] = {} /\ pinOff[l] < MaxOff - 1)
--- REPLACE
    /\ (cache[l] # {} /\ stCp[l] >= 0) \/ (cache[l] = {} /\ pinOff[l] < MaxOff - 1)
--- END

--- FIND
    /\ LiveArmed(l)
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the live advance does not exist.
    /\ FALSE
--- END
